(Flock Safety blog print capture ? Sept. 14, 2026) Tj
T*
(https://www.flocksafety.com/blog/offense-type-dropdown-a-simpler-more-accurate-audit) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Offense Type Dropdown: A Simpler, More Accurate Audit) Tj
T*
(Josh Thomas | Published: December 10, 2025 | Page also showed July 24, 2026) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We live in a time where both public safety technology and the political and legal landscape) Tj
T*
(governing public safety technology is constantly evolving. And law enforcement officers need) Tj
T*
(to balance solving cases quickly while adhering to these shifts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Our goal is to make compliance easier by building simple, built-in product features that) Tj
T*
(support consistent documentation, clearer oversight, and more confident collaboration,) Tj
T*
(without adding friction to every day workflows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Starting this week, Flock has introduced a new, required step in every ALPR Search: Offense) Tj
T*
(Type Dropdowns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This update adds a standardized, NIBRS-based offense selection \(expanded through customer) Tj
T*
(feedback and data analysis\) so agencies can capture the purpose of their search in a clear,) Tj
T*
(consistent way, while keeping searches as fast and seamless as you should always expect with) Tj
T*
(Flock.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An Offense Type for Every ALPR Search) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Beginning this week, "Offense Type" will be the first required field on any ALPR Search run) Tj
T*
(in Flock. This applies to all forms of Search - on your own cameras, on Statewide Lookup,) Tj
T*
(and on National Lookup.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The existing Search Reason field will still be available as an optional place to add extra) Tj
T*
(detail, and agencies still have the option to require it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Here's how the Offense Type Dropdown works within the search experience:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1\) Users must select at least one Offense Type before they can perform a search.) Tj
T*
(2\) Users can select multiple Offense Types when needed, but at least one is required.) Tj
T*
(3\) Users can also start typing and the relevant Offense Type will populate to maximize) Tj
T*
(speed.) Tj
T*
(4\) The admin can configure which Offense Type categories to include in the dropdown, except) Tj
T*
(where legally required to keep them all.) Tj
T*
(5\) If a user believes the Offense Type dropdown does not contain the correct description,) Tj
T*
(she can select "Other." However, if "Other" is selected, the system will require the user to) Tj
T*
(enter a Search Reason for that search, so there's always context when a standard category) Tj
T*
(doesn't apply.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Enabling Seamless Transparency) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Offense Type dropdown was designed to make documentation more consistent and oversight) Tj
T*
(more straightforward, without creating extra steps in an officer or detective's workflow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Offense Types, along with any associated Search Reasons and Case Numbers, are included in) Tj
T*
(Organization and Network Audits. Similar to Search Reason and Case Number, Offense Type can) Tj
T*
(also be included in automated Public Search Audit exports in an agency's ALPR Transparency) Tj
ET
